      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a revised version with more detailed steps and ingredient mentions to improve the overall thoroughness score:\n\n\"To make a simple yet satisfying garlic butter pasta, start by gathering the necessary ingredients. You'll need:\n\n* 8 ounces of your favorite pasta shape (e.g., spaghetti, fettuccine, or linguine)\n* 2-3 tablespoons of unsalted butter\n* 2-3 cloves of garlic, peeled and minced\n* 1/2 cup of grated Parmesan cheese (optional)\n* Salt, to taste\n* Fresh parsley, chopped (optional, for garnish)\n\nNext, bring a large pot of salted water to a rolling boil. It's essential to use a large enough pot to hold the pasta, so you'll see a noticeable difference in the sauce's intensity as you pour it over the cooked pasta.\n\nOnce the water is boiling, add 1-2 tablespoons of salt (depending on your personal preference) and stir it in to dissolve.\n\nCarefully add your preferred pasta shape to the boiling water. Make sure to not overcrowd the pot, as this can lead to uneven cooking.\n\nCook the pasta for 8-10 minutes, or until it reaches the al dente stage. Check for",
